# 4. API KEY AND EXTERNAL SERVICE REQUIREMENTS

The application should use real API integrations only where they add value.

## A. Gemini API

Use the Gemini API for:

* Natural-language equipment search.
* Alternative resource recommendations.
* Requirement extraction.
* Recommendation explanations.
* Summarisation of incident descriptions for human review.

Use the server-side secret:

GEMINI_API_KEY

Google AI Studio may configure this secret automatically when Gemini is enabled.

If it is not configured, instruct the developer to add it through the Google AI Studio Secrets settings.

Never ask users to paste the key into a frontend form.

Never expose the key in:

* React components.
* Browser JavaScript.
* Public environment variables.
* GitHub commits.
* API responses.
* Client-visible logs.

Use a currently supported Gemini model available to the project. Do not hardcode an outdated model name without checking availability.

Implement timeouts, rate limits, error handling and graceful fallback.

## B. Firebase

Use Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore.

Complete the required Firebase project setup when prompted by Google AI Studio.

Use Firebase Storage for private condition-report photographs if configured.

Do not put Firebase Admin credentials into frontend code.

## C. Optional maps integration

Do not require a maps API key for the core application.

Initially support text-based locations, institution addresses and location filters.

If Google Maps is integrated later, request the necessary API key through secure configuration, restrict the key to the intended APIs and apply appropriate usage limits.

Do not invent exact distances when reliable coordinates are unavailable.

## D. Optional external provider discovery

Build the application so an authorised external provider-discovery service can be integrated later.

Do not assume that a general search API, maps API or Gemini can provide verified rental inventory.

Do not scrape arbitrary rental websites or invent available equipment.

If no external provider API is configured, use registered ResourceLoop listings, participating institutions and community requests.

## E. Payments

For the hackathon MVP, implement rental cost calculations and payment-status records.

Do not process real money unless a payment provider is explicitly configured.

Do not collect or store card numbers, CVVs or banking passwords.

Label simulated transactions clearly.

Keep the booking lifecycle functional without requiring a payment gateway.

