# 12. IMPLEMENTATION WORKFLOW

Follow this sequence when generating the application.

Stage 1:
Create the project structure, configuration and visual design system.

Stage 2:
Build the landing page, application layout and responsive navigation.

Stage 3:
Configure Firebase Authentication and Firestore.

Stage 4:
Implement user profiles and role-based access.

Stage 5:
Implement resource creation, search and availability.

Stage 6:
Implement equipment requests and SmartFind matching.

Stage 7:
Integrate Gemini on the server side.

Stage 8:
Implement eligibility verification and booking workflows.

Stage 9:
Implement FairShare and waiting lists.

Stage 10:
Implement check-in, return, condition reporting and incident handling.

Stage 11:
Implement maintenance management and notifications.

Stage 12:
Implement analytics, administration and audit history.

Stage 13:
Create demonstration data and the full demo scenario.

Stage 14:
Run the build and tests.

Stage 15:
Fix compilation errors, broken imports, routing issues, security problems and incomplete workflows.

Stage 16:
Verify the complete end-to-end demonstration.

Do not stop after any intermediate stage if further implementation is possible.

If the project is too large to generate in one pass, create the core application first, preserve a consistent file structure, and continue through the remaining stages without replacing working functionality.

